{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226317-so-what-are-your-explanations-for-oaths-and-laws","id":1226317,"title":"So what are your explanations for Oaths and Laws?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-10T16:07:36-07:00","id":1226317,"title":"So what are your explanations for Oaths and Laws?","content":"Just a little idea I think would be fun. In the books it's pretty unknown what are Invictus Oaths and Carthian Laws, where they came from, and why they are linked to these Covenants. They are similar powers to eachother, that they literally requires one to indentify as part of their respective covenants by other members (Basically have status) and both fundamentally are based on agreement of some kind and the manipulation of that concept. Other then that tho they are so different to anything else vampires have access to, whether it's Diciplines or Blood Sorcery. So basically what my question is, that if you have one, what possible explanations and origins do you in your games ascribe to these unique supernatural powers the secular covenant seem to have a hand in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T18:29:49-07:00","id":1226346,"title":"","content":"I have them be an advanced expression of blood sympathy, more so in the case of carthian law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T04:53:18-07:00","id":1226426,"title":"","content":"Huh that totally slipped my mind. Yeah that would make sense, tho it is abit more metaphysical since while you could argue that there is a physical connection between members of clan. With Covenants it's more cognitive with only needing status. But I can definitely see that working","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:16:17-07:00","id":1226478,"title":"","content":"Are you looking for an off-game explanation or an in game one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:16:59-07:00","id":1226479,"title":"","content":"Given that Strix are able to make members of any clan there isn't as much of a physical connection as you might expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T06:59:26-07:00","id":1226759,"title":"","content":"I think the strix are smoke or vapor, not spirit.<br /> <br /> it safe to say some members of the ordo dracul have tried researching this question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T07:42:48-07:00","id":1226777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226317-so-what-are-your-explanations-for-oaths-and-laws?p=1226759#post1226759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it safe to say some members of the ordo dracul have tried researching this question?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would have, though it's a fair bet the Invictus and Carthians would resist it for fear of the powers being duplicated. In my interpretation of Requiem for Rome, the Invictus had its genesis in the Legio Mortuum, the military wing of the Roman Camarilla* - the structure of Oaths partakes both of military loyalty/unit cohesion, and oaths of initiation (paralleling the popularity of Mithraism in the Roman army). So I'd posit a very specialised kind of blood magic used by the Legio to enforce discipline and duty, repurposed by the Invictus later on. But basically that: blood magic; whatever explains it is the same as whatever explains how vampires are capable of Theban Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Carthian Law... I've got nothing. (I don't use it, so I haven't given it much thought)<br /> <br /> * I am aware the Senex had a faction called the Invictus, but they were hard core inner-circle Julii, which makes it more likely they were wiped out - the later Invictus would at most be named after them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-